  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SARA NL Lounge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The sixth edition of SARA will bring together national, regional and international stakeholders in agriculture and all its sub-sectors for ten consecutive days. It is an important gathering of international scale that brings together and exposes the agricultural expertise present in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire, the sub-region and the world.It aims to promote the production of agriculture, livestock farming, fishing, forestry, agro-food industry. The purpose of SARA is to raise awareness of the sub region&apos;s production and exchange capacity with the rest of the world, to develop technical and commercial partnerships and to provide thematic forums and symposia on agriculture and related activities.The previous edition in 2019, had 360,000 visitors with 786 exhibitors and 29 participating countries (including the Netherlands). For this sixth edition, the Ivorian Minister of Agriculture expects a strong participation from the Netherlands as Country of Honour.The SARA 2023 is focusing on the role of agricultural innovation in the fight against climate change and the post COVID recovery. The Netherlands, as second agricultural exporter in the world and leading country with regards to agricultural innovation, has a lot to offer to C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and the West African region. The Netherlands and its businesses can support C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and the West African region in its transition to a more sustainable, climate smart, innovative and circular agricultural system while at the same time also increasing yields, quality of products and profitability.This project is focusing on the trade mission from the Netherlands to the SARA. The aim of the trade mission and the Netherlands pavilion is fourfold:&#x2022;	To promote and facilitate Business-to-Business (B2B) links and knowledge transfer between Dutch companies and Ivorian/West African SMEs, companies and stakeholders, with the aim of increasing sustainable agricultural production, processing and marketing in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire/West Africa;&#x2022;	To promote selected Dutch funded programmes and activities in the agriculture sector in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and West Africa and identify new partnerships and activities;&#x2022;	To promote opportunities in C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire and in Francophone West Africa to the Dutch agricultural sector;&#x2022;	To position the Netherlands, and its companies, as the partner in sustainable, innovative and circular agriculture.</narrative>
  </description>
